# Trivy suppressions — each entry needs a reason and a review date.
#
# We still fail the pipeline on unfixed CRITICAL/HIGH findings. Entries here are
# explicitly accepted risks, not a way to silence the scanner.
#
# Review before 2027-01-31.

# spring-webmvc 6.2.x (shipped by Spring Boot 3.5.14)
#   Trivy lists 7.0.9 as the only fixed version — there is no 6.2.x fix, so these
#   cannot be cleared without a Spring Boot 4 major upgrade.
#   Exposure here is limited: the app serves JSON APIs only, no JSP/EL views, and
#   the endpoint is not internet-facing in the current deployment.
#   ACTION: revisit when Spring Boot 4.x is adopted.
CVE-2026-47884
CVE-2026-47890

# tomcat-embed-core 10.1.56
#   Advisory lists 10.1.58 as the fix, but 10.1.58 / 11.0.25 are not published
#   to Maven Central yet — 10.1.56 is the newest resolvable artefact for the
#   Spring Boot 3.5 line. Trivy's `ignore-unfixed` does not suppress this because
#   a fix version exists in the advisory database, just not in the repository.
#   ACTION: bump <tomcat.version> as soon as 10.1.58 resolves, then delete this line.
CVE-2026-65182
